# Nova - environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` at the repo root (or Config/.env). Values already set in your real
# environment win: `load_env()` never overwrites a key that already exists.
# Nothing here is required - `nova doctor` reports which engines are usable, and
# scripts/local_setup.ps1 gets a fully local stack running with no key at all.

# --- cloud engines (each one is optional; ollama has priority 1, these are 2-4) ---

# Gemini - https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Google AI Studio accepts either name; Nova checks both.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Groq - https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# OpenAI - https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- local inference (no key, this is the default path) ---

# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# --- paths ---

# Where .nova/ (settings, memory, traces) and workspace/ live. Defaults to the repo root.
# NOVA_HOME=C:\path\to\Nova-System-AI
# The sandbox the file and shell tools are confined to.
# NOVA_WORKSPACE=C:\path\to\Nova-System-AI\workspace

# --- permission gate ---

# NOVA_YOLO=1 grants write/exec/destructive actions without prompting (hard blocks
# still fire). Leave this commented out unless you are automating inside a throwaway
# VM - it applies to every run that reads this file, not just one command.
# NOVA_YOLO=1
